":"main","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","title":"worker","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","title":"threads","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","title":"code","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","title":"design","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","selector":"/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","title":"checkpoints","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"/citations/0","selector":"/citations/0","title":"Citation 1","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/1","selector":"/citations/1","title":"Citation 2","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/2","selector":"/citations/2","title":"Citation 3","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/3","selector":"/citations/3","title":"Citation 4","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/4","selector":"/citations/4","title":"Citation 5","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/5","selector":"/citations/5","title":"Citation 6","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:25","selector":"document:line:25","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:175","selector":"document:line:175","title":"4. Diagrams","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope and architectural choice align with the originating ISSUE. Both review families receive dedicated workers, durable acknowledgment precedes expensive admission, and existing projection limits, explicit recovery, trusted ownership and human approval gates remain intact. The shared host preserves family-specific coordinators without introducing another review engine. Upstream and stakeholder citations support the stated intent; no blocking defects were found in this chunk.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/4","/citations/5","document:line:25","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-e4af63128c7cbec2.json","src/daemon/threads/router.ts:246","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:61","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:78","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts:56","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts:17","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:83","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:137"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"runtime","status":"incomplete","summary":"The assigned runtime contracts preserve review identity, trusted ownership, family coordinators and explicit recovery. Two lifecycle gaps remain: crash-safe child-process reclamation lacks an implementable ownership mechanism, and the claimed startup supervision does not bound a worker that never becomes ready. Component definitions and generated source were inspected; actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"runtime-001","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5 — Worker exit and resource ownership; LLD.md:155","message":"The design requires child disposal after unexpected worker death before replacement, but delegates this to existing provider/process cleanup capabilities that cannot enforce it. runInProcessGroup owns the detached child, abort listener and exit cleanup entirely inside the calling worker; activity-mode reviews have no timeout. If that worker crashes or is terminated, main has neither a child handle nor a registered disposal operation. StartedWorker.reclaimed only covers locks and store permits. Specify a crash-surviving process ownership/disposal protocol, including spawn-registration races and confirmed disposal before releasing reservations or dispatching a replacement. Otherwise recovery must either remain fenced indefinitely or risk overlapping orphaned CLI/tool work.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md:155","src/shared/process-group.ts:108 — detached child creation and worker-local kill closure","src/shared/process-group.ts:118 — activity mode has no timeout","src/shared/process-group.ts:125 — cancellation depends on a local AbortSignal listener","src/shared/process-group.ts:143 — exit cleanup is a local child callback","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:610 — review activity execution uses runInProcessGroup","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:80 — reclamation includes locks and stores only","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — terminateAll terminates workers without child-process reclamation"]},{"id":"runtime-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/2 — Submission and acknowledgment ordering","message":"The LLD promises a named start failure when a worker never completes startup 'under existing worker startup supervision', but the reused startup path has no readiness deadline. startWorker settles only on worker-ready or exit; Supervisor adds no timeout. A live worker blocked before readiness therefore holds the submission and registry reservation indefinitely, recreating the timeout/already-running failure before durable acknowledgment. Define parent-owned bounded startup supervision, targeted termination and reclamation, late-ready rejection, and a real-worker test that never sends readiness.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md — section 3.3","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:82 — startup promise","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:86 — rejection requires worker exit","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:95 — resolution requires worker-ready","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — start and startOrReplace await startup without a deadline","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/supervisor.test.ts:215 — startup-failure coverage exercises an exiting worker","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md — acknowledgment timeout and retained reservation reproduction"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/componentDependencyDefinition","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/component-dependency.html — generated Mermaid source","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts","src/daemon/threads/channel.ts","src/daemon/threads/router.ts","src/daemon/threads/method-class.ts","src/daemon/threads/status-board.ts","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts","src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts","src/daemon/threads/worker-requests.ts","src/daemon/threads/review-state-contract.ts","src/daemon/review-request-owner.ts","src/shared/process-group.ts","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts — review subprocess and cancellation paths","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts — ownership, admission, progress and execution","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts — ownership, admission, recovery and execution","src/workflow/review/design-review/fence.ts","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-state-concurrency.test.ts","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/supervisor.test.ts — reclamation and startup-failure cases","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/ownership.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/recovery.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/controller.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/recovery.test.ts"],"limitations":["Actual rendering of docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/component-dependency.html was not verified. The rendering-tool initialization failed, and browser security policy rejected opening the local file URL. Its generated Mermaid source matches the assigned component definition; this does not establish visual correctness."],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"admission","status":"incomplete","summary":"The admission contracts preserve durable acknowledgment, immutable inputs, explicit recovery and separation from approval evidence. Existing checkpoint and progress readers require the extensions identified by the design. The generated ER model contradicts the intended ownership lifecycle. Actual diagram rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"admission-001","severity":"MED","location":"/body/erDefinition; docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html","message":"The generated ER model requires every ReviewIdentity to have exactly one ReviewWorker and exactly one ControllerOwner. This contradicts durable identities surviving worker exit and daemon-reviewed identities having no controller owner. It also renders attempts as zero-or-more despite the authored minimum cardinality of one. Correct the relationship cardinalities and regenerate the companion: a durable review has zero-or-one active worker, zero-or-one controller owner, and one-or-more persisted attempts. These are core lifecycle distinctions, particularly during interrupted admission and post-exit observation.","evidenceReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges/0 — registry entries are process-lifetime routing facts; durable reviews survive worker termination","/body/dataModelChanges/3 — daemon reviewer execution survives observer disconnect","/body/erDefinition/classes/ReviewIdentity/attributes/attempts — minimum_cardinality: 1","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html — generated Mermaid: ReviewWorker ||--|| ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html — generated Mermaid: ControllerOwner ||--o{ ReviewIdentity and ReviewIdentity ||--o{ CheckpointAttempt"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/erDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/review-worker-isolation-lld-20261109.json","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html — generated Mermaid source","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/sequence-diagram.html — generated Mermaid source","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts — admission, acknowledgment and progress","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-view.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-client.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/completion.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/contracts.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/checkpoint.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts — admission, acknowledgment, recovery and progress","src/workflow/review/design-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/read.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/approval.ts","src/mcp/code-review/schema.ts","src/mcp/design-review/schema.ts","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-state-concurrency.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/admission.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/progress-client.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/checkpoint-progress.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/correction-admission.test.ts — sequential admission and checkpoint evolution","vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts — design review fields forwarded from artifact view","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt — ArtifactReviewViewDto and parsing","vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts — review rendering contract lookup","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/review/ArtifactContentPane.kt — review rendering contract lookup"],"limitations":["Actual renderings of docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html and docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/sequence-diagram.html were not verified. The in-app browser was unavailable, and Chrome's browser security policy rejected the local file URL. Generated Mermaid source was inspected; this does not establish visual correctness."],"advice":["Make the proposed progress wire contract more concrete by naming the design admission phase and specifying how unknown task/chunk totals and admission diagnostics appear. Current code progress requires numeric totalTasks, design progress requires numeric totalChunks, and the live IDE artifact views currently carry review metadata rather than an explicit admission-progress DTO."]},{"chunkId":"evidence","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned sections align with the originating ISSUE. Recovery preserves accepted feedback, publication retries remain model-free, approval excludes unverified admission, and cleanup requires scope fencing and permanent evidence preservation. Migration covers coordinated restart, compiled-worker packaging, historical compatibility and reader-compatible rollback. No blocking defect was demonstrated in this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts — stored publication and approved-story cleanup","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts — coordinator, admission and publication wiring","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts — historical source and permanent-report requalification"