 Both review families receive dedicated workers, durable acknowledgment precedes expensive admission, and existing projection limits, explicit recovery, trusted ownership and human approval gates remain intact. The shared host preserves family-specific coordinators without introducing another review engine. Upstream and stakeholder citations support the stated intent; no blocking defects were found in this chunk.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/4","/citations/5","document:line:25","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-e4af63128c7cbec2.json","src/daemon/threads/router.ts:246","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:61","src/daemon/threads/worker-entry.ts:78","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts:56","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts:17","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:83","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:137"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"runtime","status":"incomplete","summary":"The assigned runtime contracts preserve review identity, trusted ownership, family coordinators and explicit recovery. Two lifecycle gaps remain: crash-safe child-process reclamation lacks an implementable ownership mechanism, and the claimed startup supervision does not bound a worker that never becomes ready. Component definitions and generated source were inspected; actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"runtime-001","severity":"HIGH","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/5 — Worker exit and resource ownership; LLD.md:155","message":"The design requires child disposal after unexpected worker death before replacement, but delegates this to existing provider/process cleanup capabilities that cannot enforce it. runInProcessGroup owns the detached child, abort listener and exit cleanup entirely inside the calling worker; activity-mode reviews have no timeout. If that worker crashes or is terminated, main has neither a child handle nor a registered disposal operation. StartedWorker.reclaimed only covers locks and store permits. Specify a crash-surviving process ownership/disposal protocol, including spawn-registration races and confirmed disposal before releasing reservations or dispatching a replacement. Otherwise recovery must either remain fenced indefinitely or risk overlapping orphaned CLI/tool work.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md:155","src/shared/process-group.ts:108 — detached child creation and worker-local kill closure","src/shared/process-group.ts:118 — activity mode has no timeout","src/shared/process-group.ts:125 — cancellation depends on a local AbortSignal listener","src/shared/process-group.ts:143 — exit cleanup is a local child callback","src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts:610 — review activity execution uses runInProcessGroup","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:80 — reclamation includes locks and stores only","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — terminateAll terminates workers without child-process reclamation"]},{"id":"runtime-002","severity":"MED","location":"/body/dataModelChanges/2 — Submission and acknowledgment ordering","message":"The LLD promises a named start failure when a worker never completes startup 'under existing worker startup supervision', but the reused startup path has no readiness deadline. startWorker settles only on worker-ready or exit; Supervisor adds no timeout. A live worker blocked before readiness therefore holds the submission and registry reservation indefinitely, recreating the timeout/already-running failure before durable acknowledgment. Define parent-owned bounded startup supervision, targeted termination and reclamation, late-ready rejection, and a real-worker test that never sends readiness.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md — section 3.3","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:82 — startup promise","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:86 — rejection requires worker exit","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts:95 — resolution requires worker-ready","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — start and startOrReplace await startup without a deadline","src/daemon/threads/__tests__/supervisor.test.ts:215 — startup-failure coverage exercises an exiting worker","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md — acknowledgment timeout and retained reservation reproduction"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/componentDependencyDefinition","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/0","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/1","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/2","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/3","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/4","/body/componentDependencyDefinition/components/5","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/component-dependency.html — generated Mermaid source","src/daemon/task-review-rpc.ts","src/daemon/design-review-rpc.ts","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts","