Definition; docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html","message":"The generated ER model requires every ReviewIdentity to have exactly one ReviewWorker and exactly one ControllerOwner. This contradicts durable identities surviving worker exit and daemon-reviewed identities having no controller owner. It also renders attempts as zero-or-more despite the authored minimum cardinality of one. Correct the relationship cardinalities and regenerate the companion: a durable review has zero-or-one active worker, zero-or-one controller owner, and one-or-more persisted attempts. These are core lifecycle distinctions, particularly during interrupted admission and post-exit observation.","evidenceReferences":["/body/dataModelChanges/0 — registry entries are process-lifetime routing facts; durable reviews survive worker termination","/body/dataModelChanges/3 — daemon reviewer execution survives observer disconnect","/body/erDefinition/classes/ReviewIdentity/attributes/attempts — minimum_cardinality: 1","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html — generated Mermaid: ReviewWorker ||--|| ReviewIdentity","docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/er-model.html — generated Mermaid: ControllerOwner ||--o{ ReviewIdentity and ReviewIdentity ||--o{ CheckpointAttempt"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/erDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/3","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/isolate-each-code-design-review-its-E20261109e4af6312/S001/LLD.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-e4af63128c7cbec2